  "checker_disagreement_resolutions": [
    {
      "decision_id": "primary_efflux_5125ecb5a4137fab",
      "rationale": "Reject. I independently reopened all 13 affected raw value(s) for the proposed split from `human + lactococcus lactis` to `human`, `lactococcus lactis host; human gene` and confirm the checker's disagreement: The split is exhaustive, but `ATPase assay using plasma membranes from L. Lactis overexpressing human BCRP` is assigned to `human`. The raw value explicitly states an L. Lactis expression host and a human introduced transporter, so dropping the host violates the host/gene-role rule. It needs a role-qualified label retaining the literal abbreviated host (or an approved explicit taxonomic normalization), not human alone. Because adjudication cannot rewrite labels or raw-value assignments, the proposal is rejected in full.",
      "verdict": "reject"
    },
    {
      "decision_id": "primary_efflux_aca4a50669c6b4a3",
      "rationale": "Reject. I independently reopened all 2 affected raw value(s) for the proposed rename from `zebrafish + insect` to `insect` and confirm the checker's disagreement: Both raw values explicitly state a baculovirus/insect expression system and `D. rerio Abcb4`. Renaming `zebrafish + insect` to `insect` discards the explicitly stated introduced-gene species. The supported result must retain both roles, for example `insect host; D. rerio gene` (or `insect host; zebrafish gene` only if that taxonomic normalization is explicitly approved). Because adjudication cannot rewrite labels or raw-value assignments, the proposal is rejected in full.",
      "verdict": "reject"
    },
    {
      "decision_id": "primary_efflux_db2d30fbe3300311",
      "rationale": "Reject. I independently reopened all 22 affected raw value(s) for the proposed split from `human + xenopus laevis` to `human`, `xenopus laevis`, `xenopus laevis host; human gene` and confirm the checker's disagreement: The split covers all 22 values, but `X. laevis oocytes expressing human ABCG2` and `X. laevis oocytes expressing human MDR1` are assigned to `human`. Both host and introduced-gene species are explicit in those raw values; abbreviating the host does not authorize deleting it. Those records require a role-qualified label retaining X. laevis plus human gene. Because adjudication cannot rewrite labels or raw-value assignments, the proposal is rejected in full.",
      "verdict": "reject"
    }
  ],
